From 8cd0e2cdf6983fa97085afc7d65a4aa48dc0e89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:58:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge, VideoPlayer, windowing/gbm: a base layer in HLG
 (profile 8.4) composed as one in PQ where its RPU declares that, else played
 as HLG

A Dolby Vision stream whose record says base layer signal compatibility 4
(profile 8.4: iPhone recordings among others) has a base layer in HLG,
which ETSI GS CCM 001 does not name (clause 5.2.2 a)). Nothing told the
bridge: such a picture was composed as if its base layer were in PQ,
natively and as HDR10, whatever its RPU said.

The reshaping of the RPU takes the base layer to the HDR picture that the
RPU's display management metadata describe: signal_eotf with three
parameters, and signal_bit_depth. CCM 001 sends a PQ picture with 0xFFFF,
0 0 0 and signal_bit_depth = hdr_bit_depth there (table 3, clause 6.2.2).
Read with FFmpeg's RPU parser, Dolby's profile 8.4 sample and dovi_tool's
iPhone 13 RPU both declare exactly that, and on a chart of HLG codes the
iPhone RPU's picture, read as that PQ picture, follows BT.2100's HLG to PQ
at 1000 cd/m2 (mid grey 54.6 against 53.6 cd/m2; read as HLG it would be
83 Delta E ITP off on average): the reshaping does the conversion. So:

 - DVBRIDGE::BaseLayerTransferOf() takes the place of BaseLayerIsSdr(): SDR
   in BT.1886 for compatibility 2, HLG for 4, else PQ; VideoPicture,
   the renderer's buffer and CDVBridgeGLES::Layer carry it
   (doviBaseTransfer, baseTransfer), and the bridge gives it to libplacebo
   (dvbridge_render_set_base_transfer(), pl_render_params.
   dovi_ccm_bl_transfer of libplacebo-9975), which composes a picture over
   HLG as one over PQ where its RPU declares a PQ picture, and refuses it
   otherwise, also with its own reshaping.
 - Decided before anything is drawn: the decoder reads what the RPU of
   each picture over HLG declares (DVBRIDGE::RpuDeclaresPq(),
   BaseLayerComposable()); a picture whose RPU declares another one is
   marked (VideoPicture::doviBaseRefused) and is never taken for native
   output nor reconstructed for output as HDR10 (PictureEligible(),
   WantsConversion()): it plays as Kodi plays HLG, from its base layer,
   without the two seconds of frames that cannot be shown. kodi.log says
   what the RPU declares, once each time the stream opens, and the Dolby
   Vision page gives the reason "hlgbase" (31875, en_gb and the three
   Spanish languages). (Natively the transport refused such metadata
   already, for any stream, with a reason of its own; as HDR10 it was
   composed as if PQ.) Where the bridge refuses one anyway, the reason
   of the native output given up names it ("hlgbase").
 - Every other stream is drawn as before; profile 8.2 goes through the
   same call with the same result.

Needs libplacebo-9975. Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on
lavapipe): fidbench in five configurations, the measured test with the
oracle of CCM 001 and the render test (CCM and libplacebo's reshaping)
give the same files and lines, byte for byte, as the code before this
change with the 23 patches before it. The render test with the base layer
said to be HLG on the profile 7 FEL test stream (whose RPU declares PQ)
gives the lines of the same test without it, also with the reshaping; with
its RPU declaring a gamma signal, nothing is drawn natively (the
transport's own reason) nor as HDR10 (the bridge says HLG, libplacebo why),
where before it was drawn as HDR10 as if PQ; with the base layer said to be
SDR it is composed by clause 5.5 as before. The rules of DVPlaybackPolicy.h
have a host test (21 checks).
