+/* Hades: the transfer of the base layer of the pictures that follow, as the Dolby Vision configuration
+ * of the stream says it (its base layer signal compatibility; DVBRIDGE::BaseLayerTransferOf() in Kodi):
+ *  - DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ: SMPTE ST 2084, or a compatibility that says nothing of it: composed as always;
+ *  - DVBRIDGE_BASE_SDR: SDR, in Recommendation ITU-R BT.1886 (compatibility 2: profile 8.2). ETSI GS
+ *    CCM 001 then composes its samples at 14 bits and converts them to SMPTE ST 2084 (clause 5.5),
+ *    which libplacebo does (libplacebo-9955);
+ *  - DVBRIDGE_BASE_HLG: HLG (compatibility 4: profile 8.4), which the clause does not name. Composed
+ *    as a base layer in ST 2084 where the RPU declares its HDR picture in ST 2084 at hdr_bit_depth, as
+ *    the clause sends one: the reshaping of the RPU then takes the HLG signal to that picture
+ *    (libplacebo-9975).
+ * Where libplacebo does not compose such a picture so (the setting of libplacebo's reshaping for a
+ * base layer in BT.1886, an RPU over HLG that declares another picture, or a reason that libplacebo
+ * logs), the picture is not drawn, never one composed as if its base layer were in PQ. The bridge
+ * gives libplacebo pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer. DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ when a renderer is made. */
+enum dvbridge_base_transfer {
+    DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ = 0,
+    DVBRIDGE_BASE_SDR = 1,
+    DVBRIDGE_BASE_HLG = 2,
+};
